ref 1072 #uuid "87e41470-a296-5303-9038-b8074f8d3617" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186256606 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/78/785776cee4f82c5bfa5e86b5b1cb746b7c80f2d702fb52f67055a60bdff249ae.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $(3{e}^{x}+1)\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=3{e}^{x}+1.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule for differentiation, we can rewrite this equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3{e}^{x}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we have\n\n$$\nv\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3{e}^{x}+1.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({v}^{2})=2v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x},\n$$\n\nwe can write our differential equation $(∗)$ as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=3{e}^{x}+1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259949 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of elliptic paraboloids: $z={x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+C$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186259949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07f39980-6ad0-53d7-ad63-fbb34a382f5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260057 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of elliptic cones: ${z}^{2}={x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+C$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260057 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260057 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1456f86c-f369-5c8a-aa73-f917e987fcd4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260745 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of elliptic paraboloids: $z=-{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}+C$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260745 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186260745 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64d0fc97-78ec-5077-acfa-96dd790ebb7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261222 #edb/ref 1080 "A family of planes: $z=x+3y+C$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186261222 #edb/re